cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Adaptive tree-neurons: selective conditional growth with matched allocation controls"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/adaptive-tree-neurons"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/adaptive-tree-neurons"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research software for allocating affine specialists to selected individual
  neurons through function-preserving centered-gate insertion. The implementation
  includes a residual-weighted moment score, compact PyTorch layers, matched
  random placement, ordinary growth and static gated controls, complete-state
  checkpoint recovery, source-bound experiment records and paired analysis.
  A 16-problem exploratory pilot did not establish a cheap-score advantage.
  A separate eight-problem diagnostic with two repetitions per problem found
  normalized evaluation MSE of 0.063378 for longer validation selection,
  0.063850 for random placement and 0.063125 for shorter selection. The
  descriptive interval for longer selection's mean benefit over random spans
  gains and losses. Independent prediction arithmetic and representative
  training replays agree exactly. These synthetic diagnostic results do not
  establish practical superiority, independent confirmation or model-family
  novelty. Full raw-result authentication requires the retained external
  experimental archive.
keywords:
  - neural network growth
  - conditional computation
  - capacity allocation
  - gated linear units
  - reproducible research
  - inconclusive results
